          "title": "Concepts and C++ Standards Cheatsheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Concepts (C++20)",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==concept== names a **compile-time constraint** on a type",
                "Use it as `template<Number T>`, `Number auto x`, or `requires Number<T>`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "template<typename T> concept Number = std::is_arithmetic_v<T>;",
                "template<Number T> T twice(T x);",
                "void f(Number auto x);",
                "template<typename T> requires Number<T> void g(T x);"
              ],
              "note": "three ways to apply Number"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A failed constraint gives a ==readable error==, not pages of template noise",
                "A ==requires expression== checks syntax: `requires(T a) { a + a; { a.size() } -> std::convertible_to<size_t>; }`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. What Each Standard Added",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Std",
                "Added"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{blue:C++11}",
                  "`auto`, `decltype`, range-for, lambdas, move semantics, `constexpr`, `nullptr`, smart pointers"
                ],
                [
                  "{green:C++14}",
                  "generic lambdas, `decltype(auto)`, return-type deduction"
                ],
                [
                  "{orange:C++17}",
